## Supervisor hot-path rules

- **Ingest order (oldest first):** `collect_stats_files_in_range` → `rescan_pending_stats_files` → `pending_stats_files` must be **oldest-first** (effective timestamp ascending: filename epoch when numeric, else mtime; `None` sort keys last). The supervisor ingests from the queue head (`pending_stats_files[:chunk_size]`). `cap_pending_stats_file_list` must retain the **oldest** `max_size` entries when truncating (drop newer paths). Do not reverse to newest-first without an explicit product decision and regression tests. **Incremental rescan** must **merge** newly discovered paths into existing `pending_stats_files` (`merge_rescan_discovered_into_pending`), not replace the queue with a partial host-dir subset. **Queue mutations** (handoff prepend, checkpoint-blocked prepend, failed-chunk requeue) must use `sort_pending_stats_paths_oldest_first`, not lexicographic path sort. **Tar-aligned unprocessed only:** `oldest_checkpoint_incomplete_tar`, day-close `checkpoint_incomplete`, and `classify_day_close_candidates` `unprocessed=` count only paths whose filename/mtime calendar day maps to that tar (`aligned_on_disk_unprocessed_paths_for_tar`). Cross-day misbuckets (first_ts map key ≠ filename day) must **not** pin `oldest_tar` or block day-close for the wrong calendar day; report them as `unprocessed_cross_day_n` when present. **Report `checkpoint_incomplete` only when aligned on-disk unprocessed > 0** (never for ghosts/cross-day alone). Every on-disk mutable `YYYY-MM-DD.tar` is a report candidate (`mutable_tar=yes` / reason `mutable_tar_present`); aligned=0 + needs work → `ready_for_enqueue` (not `disqualified`) so discover can enqueue. **Candidate log lines** print **oldest calendar day first** regardless of status; **`queue_order=1..N` only for `status=queued`** (oldest queued first), else **`queue_order=`**. Discover logs `ready_for_enqueue_n` and counts `skipped_inflight` only among ready entries. **Pending cap:** `_cap_pending_after_rescan` must merge **all** days’ on-disk unprocessed into pending before oldest-first truncate (not only the oldest_tar reserved set). **`supplement_pending_paths_from_closed_paths`:** when the queue is already at `max_size`, still union snapshot `closed_paths`, sort oldest-first, and recap so older paths **replace** newer heads — log `pending cap supplement replace`. **`select_ingest_chunk_paths`:** gate uses aligned blocked paths only; when fallback would dispatch **cross_day_bucket-only** blocked paths while `pending` is non-empty, **defer** and return `pending[:chunk]` — log `oldest_day_chunk_gate_cross_day_defer`.
- **No blocking maintenance** on the supervisor thread: do not reintroduce `_archive_maintenance_pipeline`, forced two-phase maintenance, supervisor-driven seal/raw/`.tar` bursts, or steady-state **`run_supervisor_day_raw_removal_delete_pass`** between chunks.
- **Startup (`startdate == 'all'` only):** `archive_janitor.enqueue_startup_debt()` signals janitor work only (no unparsable tree scan); `signal_scheduled_maintenance_pass(reason="startup")` queues the janitor heavy maintenance pass, which runs **`_discover_and_enqueue_ready_day_close(reason="startup")`** on the **janitor thread** (cap **`sync_day_close_max_inflight`**, default **4** — same as steady-state). **Heavy/startup pass must share one `classify_day_close_candidates`** between the candidate report and discover (`_build_day_close_candidate_entries` → report + discover `entries=`); do not double-classify (~2× wall) on boot. Regression: **`test_heavy_pass_classifies_day_close_candidates_once`**. **`_close_one_day` execution** is deferred until supervisor **`get_startup_ingest_gate_cleared()`** returns true (`janitor: tick deferred day_close_execution reason=startup_prep`). Ingest is **never** gated on day-close completion. Boot handoff discover runs **once** at the first main-loop iteration after gate clear via **`_process_boot_handoffs_once()`** (not during the startup prep block). Quiescent dirty `.tar` days enqueue via janitor discover (`awaiting_janitor_discover`). Unparseable closed raw is quarantined at ingest parse failure (`quarantine_ingest_failed_raw_path`). Date-range runs without **`all`** skip this startup block.
- **Chunk end (ingest-only):** after each chunk — `_finalize_archive_slots_if_needed(context="end_of_batch")`, **`archive_janitor.signal_work_available()`**, **`_maybe_enqueue_immediate_day_close(context="chunk_end")`** (async submit only). **`_should_defer_immediate_day_close`** must defer at **`chunk_end`** (and all immediate contexts) when **`handoff_priority_paths`** is non-empty — MainThread must not run synchronous **`requeue_closed_raw_paths_for_ingest`** while handoff is draining (RC-F two-queue law). On defer: log `immediate day_close defer context=…`, run **`_reconcile_pending_with_oldest_checkpoint_incomplete`**, and only flush deferred **`archive_finalize`** day_close when handoff queue is empty. Optional periodic **rescan** at `chunk_counter % rescan_every_chunks == 0` uses **`_rescan_processed_exclusions()`** — **does not** call `signal_scheduled_maintenance_pass` at chunk boundary.
- **Idle / empty queue:** `signal_work_available()` when pending drains; `_maybe_enqueue_immediate_day_close(context="idle_finalize")` on rescan-with-no-work paths.
- **`archive_maintenance_interval_seconds`:** deprecated and ignored; do not reintroduce interval accrual on the supervisor.
- **Finalize:** `force=True` with `allow_defer=True` when backlog present; log `Archive finalize deferred` instead of blocking ingest. **`post_finalize_reconcile`** runs inline in **`_apply_archive_finalize_results`** (not at chunk start).
- **Shutdown:** `archive_janitor.shutdown(wait=True)` in supervisor `finally`.

## Day-close debt (disk-critical)

Canonical per-calendar-day pipeline debt is **`DebtKind.DAY_CLOSE`**: one heap item runs seal → verify → **batch delete** (when preflight on) → `.tar` drop for a single daily `.tar` within tick budget; partial progress re-enqueues `DAY_CLOSE`.

**Enqueue paths (oldest first where applicable):**

- **Proactive discover (every tick):** `_discover_and_enqueue_ready_day_close` at the start of **`_run_tick_body`** (`reason=tick`) and after light/heavy maintenance passes. Checkpoint-complete days with classify status **`ready_for_enqueue`** (reason **`awaiting_janitor_discover`**) enqueue **`DAY_CLOSE`** debt up to **`sync_day_close_max_inflight`** (default **4** = pipeline occupancy **and** parallel worker pool size). When enqueue fails without hitting max-inflight, log **`janitor: discover_enqueue_reject tar=… reason=…`** and include **`skipped_eligible=N`** in the discover summary (distinct from **`skipped_inflight`**). Common reject reasons: **`already_on_debt_heap`**, submit **`checkpoint_incomplete`**, manifest **`disqualified`**. **Mid-tick refill:** when **`_pop_one_day_close_debt`** returns empty and **`_day_close_free_slots() > 0`**, discover runs again with **`reason=tick_slot_free`** and optional **`slot_budget=free_slots`**. Regression: **`test_discover_logs_enqueue_reject_when_submit_ineligible`**, **`test_discover_logs_already_on_debt_heap`**, **`test_janitor_tick_discovers_and_submits_without_startup_reason`**, **`test_janitor_startup_tick_discovers_and_enqueues_day_close`**, **`test_no_async_day_close_worker_submit_on_discover`**, **`test_janitor_runs_multiple_day_close_in_parallel`**, **`test_janitor_refills_slot_when_one_day_close_finishes`**, **`test_mid_tick_discover_enqueues_when_heap_empty_and_slots_free`**, **`test_discover_enqueues_when_debt_heap_full_but_no_live_workers`**.
- **Scheduled scan:** `run_scheduled_maintenance_pass` on the **janitor thread** when supervisor signals **`reason=startup`** at boot or other non-chunk-boundary maintenance reasons. **No longer** triggered every N ingest chunks or on every ingest-queue drain at chunk boundary. Light/heavy passes refresh candidate report + run the same discover helper (no **`eligible_deferred`** limbo).
- **Calendar-day ingest drain (immediate):** supervisor `_maybe_enqueue_immediate_day_close` after **`chunk_end`**, **`archive_finalize`** (inline reconcile first), and **`idle_finalize`**. Enqueues janitor **`DAY_CLOSE`** via **`archive_janitor._enqueue_eligible_day_close`** / manifest shim — not blocked by unrelated `pending_stats_files` on other days. On defer after archive finalize: **`signal_work_available()`** only (no **`archive_finalize_deferred`** maintenance reason).
- **Seal disqualification:** `build_day_close_disqualified_daily_tars` — inflight append, append cache, in-flight archive jobs, pending archive tasks, unmapped closed raw. **`pending_stats_paths` must never** appear in seal disqualifiers.
- **Delete disqualification (strict superset):** `_janitor_delete_disqualified_daily_tars()` unions seal disqualifiers with daily `.tar` for any path in **`handoff_priority_paths`**, lock-snapshotted **`pending_stats_paths`**, **all** active chunk in-flight paths via **`_IngestPoolInFlightTracker.all_in_flight_paths()`** (not **`sample_in_flight(10)`**), and **`chunk_dispatch_paths`** for the current chunk. Janitor **`_close_one_day`** skips batch delete when `tar_norm ∈ delete_disqualified`; re-enqueues `DAY_CLOSE`.
- **Path-level delete guard (manifest-verified):** **`apply_batch_delete`** uses **`_get_ingest_active_skip_paths()`** (no `paths_pending_delete`) before **`os.remove`**, or subtracts own-day `paths_pending_delete()` from quarantine when unwired. Verify keeps full **`get_quarantine_skip_paths()`**. When a path remains ingest-active, log **`janitor: day_close delete defer tar=… day=… path=… reason=active_ingest skip_class=…`**, set manifest **`delete_deferred=active_ingest`**, and retry on a later tick. Regression: **`test_apply_batch_delete_deletes_when_only_in_paths_pending_delete`**, **`test_apply_batch_delete_skips_path_in_quarantine_skip_paths`**, **`test_arch_apply_batch_delete_rechecks_quarantine_skip_paths`**, **`test_arch_delete_disqualified_uses_full_inflight_not_sample`**.
- **Submit eligibility:** `daily_tar_eligible_for_day_close_submit` uses **`unprocessed_tar_paths_still_on_disk`** for checkpoint-complete gating only (no closed-raw submit gate).
- **Oldest-day pending reconcile:** before each ingest chunk, supervisor prepends on-disk checkpoint-blocked paths for the **single oldest** calendar day. Snapshot precedence: startup coordinator → janitor accrual → live fallback.
- **Janitor-thread verify/delete:** **`ArchiveJanitor._close_one_day`** runs **pre-seal verify (open `.tar`) → dedupe → seal → post-seal parity verify → `begin_deleting` + `apply_batch_delete`** when verify stages complete and not delete-disqualified. Retryable pre-seal paths hand off to ingest **before seal**. **Seal is not gated on closed-raw presence** (verified closed-raw remains on disk until post-seal delete); closed-raw safety is **pre-seal + handoff** before seal and **`_tar_drop_one_day`** / **`blocking_closed_raw_remains_for_day`** (alias `remaining_raw_blocking_day_incomplete`) after delete. No `ignore_remaining_raw` parameter. Steady-state supervisor **does not** call **`run_supervisor_day_raw_removal_delete_pass`**. Regression: **`test_arch_steady_state_ingest_not_gated_on_raw_deletion`**, **`test_arch_no_raw_delete_pending_in_steady_state_tree`**, **`test_arch_janitor_close_one_day_owns_delete_not_supervisor`**, **`test_arch_day_close_verify_before_seal`**, **`test_close_one_day_seals_when_remaining_raw_on_disk_after_pre_seal`**.
- **Filesystem-truth manifest `complete`:** `is_complete` / manifest **`status=complete`** require **`_day_close_filesystem_complete`** / shared **`day_close_filesystem_complete`**. Stale complete downgraded on init/recover. **`daily_tar_needs_day_close_work`** returns False for sealed-only + no **blocking** remaining even without a `tar_dropped` phase hint.
- **Remaining-raw law:** **census** (`build_remaining_raw_*`) is inventory/verify worklists/logging only. **Every DECISION gate** (tar_drop, seal retain, needs_work, decompress-unlink, filesystem-complete) uses **`remaining_raw_blocking_day_incomplete`** / quarantine-aware blockers. **Blocking paths must be tar-aligned** (filename/mtime calendar day maps to the daily tar — same as checkpoint unprocessed); first_ts misbuckets under the wrong tar key are **`processed_cross_day_n`** diagnostics only and must **not** reopen / block that calendar day. Candidate lines print **`processed_but_on_disk=`** (aligned leftover closed raw) and optional **`processed_cross_day_n=`**. Tar already gone + sealed → mark `tar_dropped` (no false `waiting_on_ingest` defer when `handoff_paths=0`).
- **Closed raw handoff:** **`requeue_closed_raw_paths_for_ingest`** before kick; rescan uses **`rescan_exclude_paths()`** — see supervisor handoff helpers in **`sync_timedb.py`** and **`sync-timedb-canonical-startup-archive-scan.mdc`**.
- **Ghost delete / stale done:** **`reopen_done_days_with_verified_on_disk()`** and **`reopen_stale_done_all_skipped()`** on janitor tick before delete; reopen clears **`verify_stage`** (must not leave **`phase=verifying` + `verify_stage=post_seal_complete`**). **`promote_phase_if_verify_stage_ahead`** in **`_close_one_day`** promotes that inconsistent pair to **`verification_complete`** before delete (never silent re-enqueue). Manifest-fast **`phase=done`** with retryable skips on disk still handoffs via ingest. When **`delete_phase_done`**, run **`reclassify_retryable_skips_after_handoff_sync`** **before** reopen helpers so mixed manifests and post-handoff stale skips upgrade without **`reopen_stale_done_all_skipped`** forcing full reverify; then **`begin_deleting` + `apply_batch_delete`** when upgrades occur. Upgrades stale **`skipped_not_in_archive`** (and other retryable skips) to **`verified`** before tar-drop. **`kick_closed_raw_unblock`** uses the same reclassify when all blockers are retryable. **`_record_entry`** adjusts **`skipped_count`/`verified_count`** on skip→verified upgrade. Tar-drop defer logs **`reason=stale_manifest_retryable`** when **`phase=done`** with retryable manifest paths (not misleading **`waiting_on_ingest`**).
- **Waiting-on-ingest predicates (quarantine transparent):** **`_manifest_only_waiting_on_ingest`** / **`_only_waiting_on_ingest_blocks_completion`** treat **`skipped_quarantine`** as transparent — every on-disk entry must be retryable **or** quarantine-terminal, with **≥1** retryable remaining. Mixed **`skipped_not_in_archive` + `skipped_quarantine`** after verified delete → **`_mark_done_waiting_on_ingest`** + handoff (not stuck **`verification_complete`** reseal). Quarantine-only still uses **`_finalize_quarantine_terminal_done`**. Regression: **`test_mixed_not_in_archive_and_quarantine_marks_done_waiting_on_ingest`**, **`test_promote_phase_when_verifying_but_post_seal_complete`**, **`test_close_one_day_promotes_verifying_post_seal_and_deletes_or_handoffs`**.
- **In-progress verify:** janitor re-enqueues `DAY_CLOSE` while async verify incomplete.
- **Batch delete driver (preflight on):** **`ArchiveJanitor._close_one_day`** after `verification_complete` calls `begin_deleting` + `apply_batch_delete` when not delete-disqualified — **not** MainThread chunk loop. Delete-disqualified paths log durable **`janitor: day_close delete deferred … reason=delete_disqualified`**. On successful tar-drop / FS complete, **`_finalize_day_close_manifest`** calls **`finalize_complete_if_filesystem`** so manifest reaches **`complete`** (not only startup delete pass).
- **Discover cap (enqueue limit):** **`DayCloseManifestCoordinator.active_discover_cap_tar_paths(live_worker_tars=...)`** = live **`_day_close_in_flight`** workers ∪ manifest worker-slot statuses (`submitted`, `queued`, `sealing`, `raw_removal`) — **excludes** debt heap and manifest **`deferred` / `waiting_on_ingest`**. Used for **`_discover_and_enqueue_ready_day_close`** and supervisor **`_maybe_enqueue_immediate_day_close`**. Discover log includes **`active_workers`**, **`deferred_waiting`**, **`debt_heap`**, **`manifest_pending`**, **`discover_cap`**, **`worker_occupancy`** (legacy metric), and **`free_slots=`** when **`reason=tick_slot_free`**. Regression: **`test_discover_enqueues_when_deferred_waiting_on_ingest_not_worker_inflight`**, **`test_active_worker_tar_paths_excludes_deferred_waiting_on_ingest`**, **`test_discover_cap_excludes_debt_heap_from_inflight`**, **`test_discover_enqueues_when_debt_heap_full_but_no_live_workers`**.
- **Legacy worker occupancy (reporting):** **`active_worker_tar_paths()`** = discover cap ∪ debt heap **`DAY_CLOSE`** (minus deferred) — for operator correlation only; **not** used for discover cap. **`_day_close_worker_occupancy_tar_paths()`** on the janitor delegates to this legacy metric.
- **Ghost manifest reconcile (before discover):** each tick **reap completed day-close futures**, then **`recover_stale_manifest_entries()`** + **`reconcile_manifest_with_debt_heap(debt_tar_paths, live_worker_tars)`** **before** **`_discover_and_enqueue_ready_day_close(reason=tick)`** so discover_cap is not filled by ghost pending rows. Reconcile re-enqueues manifest worker slots with no heap debt and no live worker. **`enqueue_day_close`**: pending manifest row without heap debt falls through to **`enqueue_day_close_fn`** (not silent `True`). **`defer_for_ingest_handoff`**: creates **`deferred/waiting_on_ingest`** row when missing. Regression: **`test_janitor_reconcile_before_discover_order`**, **`test_enqueue_day_close_requeues_when_manifest_queued_without_debt`**, **`test_reconcile_manifest_ghost_slot_downgrades_or_reenqueues`**, **`test_defer_for_ingest_handoff_creates_entry_when_missing`**.
- **Candidate counters (three-way census):** **`on_disk`** = total aligned closed-raw still on disk for that tar; **`unprocessed`** = subset not checkpoint-complete; **`processed_but_on_disk`** = subset that is checkpoint-complete leftover. Invariant: **`on_disk = unprocessed + processed_but_on_disk`**. Do **not** reprint `unprocessed` as `on_disk`. **`queued`** status ≠ live day-close workers. Regression: **`test_classify_on_disk_equals_unprocessed_plus_processed`**, **`test_classify_reports_processed_but_on_disk_and_cross_day`**.
- **Candidate / operator inflight (honest pending):** **`_day_close_active_tar_paths()`** = live day-close workers ∪ debt heap **`DAY_CLOSE`** ∪ manifest **worker-slot** statuses (`queued`/`submitted`/`sealing`/`raw_removal` via **`manifest_worker_slot_tar_paths`**) — **excludes** manifest **`deferred` / `waiting_on_ingest`** so handoff-deferred days can classify as **`ready_for_enqueue`** after ingest advances (not stuck `queued`/`day_close_in_progress` with `active_workers=0`). Used for classify **`day_close_in_progress`** only, **not** discover cap. **`get_inflight_tar_paths_fn`** on the manifest shim reads debt heap only (no recursion). Regression: **`test_day_close_active_tar_paths_excludes_deferred_waiting_on_ingest`**.
- **Misbucket handoff pin:** supervisor **`age_misbucket_handoff_priority_paths`** drops **`handoff_priority_paths`** whose derived calendar day has **`no_daily_archive`** (neither sealed nor mutable tar), logs **`handoff_priority_age path=… source_day=… derived_day=…`**, clears deferred on the source tar, and signals janitor. **`select_ingest_chunk_paths`** also skips such cross-day leads (`handoff_cross_day_skip … reason=no_daily_archive`). Must not permanently pin every chunk or forever defer immediate day_close. Regression: **`test_select_ingest_chunk_skips_misbucket_handoff_without_daily_archive`**, **`test_age_misbucket_handoff_priority_paths_clears_and_returns_source`**.
- **Discover ready→start:** when classify reports **`ready_for_enqueue_n≥1`** and **`free_slots>0`**, discover must enqueue (`enqueued>0`) or log durable **`discover_enqueue_reject`**; tick must not end forever with **`days_started=0`** solely because deferred handoff polluted classify in-progress. Soft wait (`waiting_on_ingest` / `checkpoint_incomplete` with **`unprocessed>0`**) remains correct.
- **Manifest enqueue ordering:** **`enqueue_day_close`** persists manifest **`queued`** only **after** successful **`enqueue_day_close_fn`** (no orphan pending on enqueue failure).

**Legacy hints/debt:** persisted `SEAL_PRIOR_DAY` / `RAW_REMOVE` / `TAR_DROP` for the same `tar_path` coalesce to one `DAY_CLOSE` on load and when popped for a tick.

This must **not** wait for an empty global ingest queue.

## Tar retention (default reclaim)

- **`archive_keep_uncompressed_tar=no`** (default): prior-calendar-day `.tar` may be dropped at seal when closed raw is gone (`effective_keep_uncompressed_tar` → `atomic_seal_tar_to_zst` `keep_tar=False`).
- **Calendar today:** do not **start** sealing until **`archive_today_uncompressed_tar_grace_hours`** (default **8**) after local midnight (`daily_tar_seal_calendar_eligible`). After seal, keep uncompressed `.tar` during the same grace window (`effective_keep_uncompressed_tar`) unless global keep is `yes`.
- **`archive_keep_uncompressed_tar=yes`:** always retain `.tar` until explicit `TAR_DROP` / day-close tail.
- **Ghost `remaining_raw_by_gz` gate:** **`blocking_closed_raw_remains_for_day`** / **`remaining_raw_by_gz_has_paths_on_disk`** (census inventory) — **blocking** map for **tar-drop** and scheduling; census for snapshots/logging only. Hint `tar_dropped` / manifest `phase=done` must not skip disk predicate (RC-L).
- **Immediate day-close inflight:** respects **`sync_day_close_max_inflight`** via **`active_discover_cap_tar_paths()`** (live workers + manifest worker slots — not debt heap, not deferred handoff).
- **Tar drop deferred logging:** **`_tar_drop_one_day`** logs **`handoff_paths=N`** when raw stats block unlink (correlates with ingest handoff stall).

## Janitor tick (`ArchiveJanitor._run_tick_body`)

- **Startup prep gate:** after scheduled maintenance and **`_discover_and_enqueue_ready_day_close`**, when **`get_startup_ingest_gate_cleared()`** is false, log **`janitor: tick deferred day_close_execution reason=startup_prep`** and **return before** the debt-drain worker loop (`_close_one_day`). Discover/enqueue still runs; persisted debt from hints v2 is subject to the same defer. Regression: **`test_janitor_tick_defers_day_close_execution_before_ingest_gate_cleared`**, **`test_janitor_startup_tick_discovers_and_enqueues_day_close`**.
- **Drain within budget (non-blocking after budget_exit):** within one `signal_work_available` wake, reconcile then **`_discover_and_enqueue_ready_day_close(reason=tick)`**, fill a day-close worker pool (up to **`sync_day_close_max_inflight`**), and refill free slots via **`wait(..., FIRST_COMPLETED)`** until the heap is empty **or** **`archive_janitor_budget_seconds`** expires. While-condition uses **`_day_close_free_slots() > 0`** (global **`_day_close_in_flight`** truth). Same calendar day is not re-popped within one tick after a partial/failed attempt. **On `budget_exit`:** do **not** drain-wait remaining day-close futures (operator failure class: **`duration_s=9217`** after `budget_exit` with `days_completed=0`). Leave futures in **`_day_close_in_flight`**, log **`janitor: tick budget_exit leave_in_flight=N`**, and schedule follow-up; cross-tick reap + fill + **`future.add_done_callback` → `signal_work_available`**. **Budget-wait visibility:** while waiting **within** budget, emit **`janitor: tick waiting in_flight=N debt_remaining=M tars=…`** at most every **300s**. **Seal / tar-drop failure:** **`_enqueue_day_close` + `_persist_hints`** before returning `False`. Regression: **`test_janitor_budget_exit_nonblocking_leaves_in_flight`**, **`test_janitor_tick_wait_heartbeat`**, **`test_arch_janitor_drains_multiple_enqueued_jobs_per_wake`**, **`test_janitor_tick_discovers_and_submits_without_startup_reason`**, **`test_janitor_refills_slot_when_one_day_close_finishes`**, **`test_day_close_parallel_respects_max_inflight`**, **`test_day_close_free_slots_excludes_running_workers`**, **`test_fill_free_slots_submits_to_idle_workers_while_others_running`**, **`test_seal_failure_and_tar_drop_unlink_failure_reenqueue`**.
- **Tick chaining:** when budget breaks mid-drain with **`debt_depth() > 0` or in-flight day-close remain**, and **`(tick_made_progress or tick_mutated or budget_throttled_this_tick or has_in_flight)`**, **`_pending_signal`** schedules follow-up tick; log **`janitor: tick budget_exit debt_remaining=N scheduling_followup=yes`**. Regression: **`test_janitor_budget_partial_tick_schedules_followup`**, **`test_janitor_budget_exit_nonblocking_leaves_in_flight`**.
- **Maintenance vs debt budget:** `run_scheduled_maintenance_pass` runs before debt drain; **debt-drain budget starts after maintenance** (burst/idle/ingest-priority scale **budget only**).
- Coordinator single-flight `ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=1)` for the janitor wake; thread title `sync_timedb.py [thread:archive-janitor]`. Day-close workers use `sync_timedb.py [thread:day-close-N]` and call **`close_old_connections()`** entry/finally.
- Guard `_debt_heap` / `_debt_seen` with `_debt_lock`; accrual and ticks share the same lock.
- Per tick: RSS pre-check → fill free slots → process **`DAY_CLOSE`** on the worker pool within budget.
- **Mid-tick disqualification:** recompute **`get_disqualified_daily_tars()`** (seal) before each debt item; use **`get_delete_disqualified_daily_tars()`** for delete decisions inside **`_close_one_day`**.
- **Post-seal cleanup (always on):** janitor-thread two-stage verify then **`begin_deleting` + `apply_batch_delete`** in **`_close_one_day`**. **`sync_day_close_raw_removal_preflight`** removed — no legacy **`_raw_remove_one_day`** incremental path.
- **Hints:** guard `_validated_days` / `_day_phases` with `_hints_state_lock`; set **`day_phases`** only when disk predicate passes for that step. Serialize disk persist with **`_persist_hints_lock`** (outermost in **`_persist_hints`**, held through snapshot + **`save_archive_maint_hints`**) so parallel **`day-close-N`** workers and the janitor tick do not race the shared hints file; unique temp files in **`_save_json_atomic`** (`sync_timedb_persistence.py`) eliminate fixed-**`.tmp`** ENOENT on concurrent writers.
- **Budget/exception:** re-queue incomplete days; never drop tail debt on budget break or tick exception; do not busy-spin the same day within one tick.
- **Fresh per-day raw:** `build_remaining_raw_for_daily_tar` for keep_tar at seal and for `TAR_DROP` remaining-raw gate (seal itself does not defer on closed-raw).
- **DAY_CLOSE on worker threads:** pre-seal verify → seal → post-seal verify → delete → tar_drop in **`_close_one_day`**; manifest coordinator records progress only. Re-enqueue until filesystem complete (next tick). Pre-seal complete resumes at seal (no full re-verify).
- **Full** `build_archive_maintenance_snapshot` on **heavy** passes only (`reason=startup`, `reason=day_ingest_complete:<date>` when explicitly signaled — not from chunk boundary).
- **Lock cleanup:** per tick with day-pipeline debt — manifest-dir orphan cleanup only on startup heavy pass; non-startup heavy passes run stale lock cleanup on archive + daily dirs.
- **Dedupe:** `_consume_dedupe_hints` + inline dedupe before seal; invalidate L1 + Redis on mutation.
- **Hot-path lock priority:** ingest/populate/append wins over janitor dedupe/seal/delete on shared daily tar fnctl locks — see **`sync-timedb-hot-path-janitor-lock-priority.mdc`**. Janitor **defers** before write and **cooperatively yields** mid-dedupe/zstd when ingest signals (`ingest_tar_hot`, populate lock, `signal_day_close_yield`). **Exception:** daily tar restore from sealed (`daily_tar_restore` Redis key) runs to completion; populate **waits** (`populate: wait daily_tar_restore`). Operator grep: `janitor: day_close defer|yield`, `defer_cap_exceeded`.
- `close_old_connections()` at tick entry and in `finally`.

## Pool lifecycle and parallelism (2026-07)

Canonical reference: **`docs/SYNC_TIMEDB_PARALLELISM.md`**.

| Category | Examples | Policy |
|----------|----------|--------|
| **Hot-path spawn pools** | `ingest_pool`, `db_writer_pool`, `archive_pool`, sealed-archive CLI pool | Stay on **spawn**; created via `create_sync_timedb_spawn_pool()`; distinct initializers per pool kind |
| **Session thread executors** | `ArchiveJanitor`, startup preflights, `DayRawRemovalCoordinator` | **Eager** `SessionSingleFlightExecutor(max_workers=1)` when role enabled; shutdown in supervisor `finally` |
| **Ephemeral burst threads** | metadata reads, parallel seal/validation/migrate | `run_bounded_thread_pool()` / `iter_bounded_thread_pool()`; not session-static |
| **Subprocess CLI** | zstd, GNU `tar -r` | Not Python pools |

**Normalization allowed:** shared spawn factory, session executor helper, burst thread helper — **no behavior change** on hot-path dispatch.

**Forbidden without explicit approval + regression battery:**

- Ingest or archive hot path Pool → threads (`map_async` / `imap_unordered_watch_pool` semantics differ from `Future` submit).
- Janitor tick → spawn process (violates two-queue single-flight law).
- Renaming `archive_pool` log label without operator doc sync.

**Archive pool on spawn (documented rationale):** append is I/O-heavy but spawn retains per-job process recycle, failure isolation, and L1 cache benefits; default inflight is low (`sync_archive_max_inflight_jobs`).

## Scheduled maintenance pass

- **Supervisor signals only:** `signal_scheduled_maintenance_pass(reason)` sets pending flag and `signal_work_available()`; no snapshot on MainThread.
- **Janitor thread:** `run_scheduled_maintenance_pass` → heavy or light pass.
- **Heavy triggers:** `reason=startup`; `reason=day_ingest_complete:<YYYY-MM-DD>` when explicitly queued (not from per-chunk supervisor hook after 2026-06 refactor).
- **Heavy defer:** re-queues when chunk in progress or ingest pool in-flight > 0.
- **Light triggers:** enqueue-only maintenance reasons (not **`every_n_chunks`** / **`ingest_queue_empty`** at chunk boundary). Discover runs at end of light pass.
- **Burst / idle bonus:** unchanged (`archive_janitor_debt_high_watermark`, `archive_maintenance_idle_seconds`).

## Forbidden patterns

- Blocking supervisor seal/raw/`.tar` maintenance or steady-state **`run_supervisor_day_raw_removal_delete_pass`** in the chunk loop.
- **`signal_scheduled_maintenance_pass`** every N chunks or on every chunk-end queue drain (archival scheduling belongs to enqueue + janitor drain).
- Treating `pending_stats_files == 0` as the **only** path to enqueue day-close debt during multi-week backlog.
- Enqueuing three separate `SEAL`/`RAW`/`TAR` debts per day in new code (use `DAY_CLOSE`).
- Delete for a calendar day while **`handoff_priority_paths`** or same-day pending/inflight ingest overlap (**`delete_disqualified`** must block).
- Marking manifest **`phase=done`** or hint **`tar_dropped`** when verified/skipped paths or `.tar` still exist on disk without reopen (RC-I/L).
- Silent debt drop at `archive_janitor_debt_max_entries`.
- Dropping unprocessed debt on budget expiry or tick exception.
- `TAR_DROP` / day-close tail with stale `remaining_raw_by_gz` when closed raw may exist on disk.

## Append dispatch

- Up to `sync_archive_max_inflight_jobs` disjoint daily-tar `map_async` slots via `ArchiveDispatchCoordinator`.
- At capacity, `stats["queued"]` must equal batch size once (not per-item inflation).
- Log stall once per slot when elapsed ≥ `sync_archive_worker_stall_seconds` and job not `ready()`.

## Data safety (unchanged)

- DB head-ingest gate before raw delete/append when `sync_archive_require_db_ingest=yes`.
- Seal-before-delete per day; shrink guard; zst-then-gz corrupt tar restore; member-map zstd skip equivalence.
- Default `sync_enable_ingest_first_durability_mode=yes` (checkpoint after DB).

